@node Overview
@chapter Overview

The @samp{tlon-ai} module integrates AI capabilities into the Tlon editorial workflow. It leverages the @samp{gptel} package to communicate with various large language model backends (OpenAI, Gemini, and others) for tasks that span the full content lifecycle: summarization and abstract generation, translation, reference article creation and proofreading, Markdown formatting restoration, phonetic transcription, mathematical expression handling, meta description and title generation, language detection, commit diff summarization, and cross-repository change propagation.

A key design principle is that each task can use a dedicated AI model, letting you pair computationally demanding tasks (such as book-length summarization) with large-context models and more routine tasks with faster, cheaper alternatives. The module also supports batch processing of Bib@TeX{} entries and offers a comprehensive transient menu (@ref{Transient menu, , transient menu}) for quick access to all operations.

