@node Batch processing function
@subsection Batch processing function

@vindex tlon-ai-batch-fun
The user option @code{tlon-ai-batch-fun} specifies which function to call when processing Bib@TeX{} entries in batch mode. You can set it interactively from the transient menu (@ref{Transient menu, , transient menu}) via the @samp{s -b} infix. Set it to @samp{nil} to disable batch processing.

Typical values include @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-or-without-ai}, @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai}, @code{tlon-fetch-and-set-abstract}, and @code{tlon-ai-set-language-bibtex}. The default value is @samp{nil}.

When @code{tlon-ai-batch-fun} is set to one of the three abstract-related commands and the command is invoked interactively from a Bib@TeX{} buffer, it delegates to @code{tlon-batch-set-abstracts} (see the @samp{tlon-bib} manual, @ref{h:batch-set-abstracts,Batch set abstracts,,tlon-bib,}) with the matching strategy (@samp{non-ai}, @samp{ai}, or @samp{both}). The batch runs in the background on a hidden copy of the file, so the current Emacs session is not interrupted: the buffer is not widened, point does not jump, and progress is written to @samp{*tlon-batch-abstract-log*} instead of the echo area.

For the legacy function @code{tlon-ai-set-language-bibtex}, the older per-entry iteration driven by @code{tlon-ai-batch-continue} continues to apply.

Because the overwrite infix (@samp{s -o}, @code{tlon-abstract-overwrite}) still controls collisions and its @samp{ask} value prompts mid-run, set it to @samp{always} or @samp{never} when you want an unattended batch.

@node Editing prompts before sending
@subsection Editing prompts before sending

@vindex tlon-ai-edit-prompt
When the user option @code{tlon-ai-edit-prompt} is non-nil, every AI prompt is presented in the minibuffer for editing before it is sent to the model. This is useful for one-off adjustments---for example, adding clarifying context or constraining the output format---without modifying the underlying prompt constants. The default value is @samp{nil}.

@node Automatic proofreading of reference articles
@subsection Automatic proofreading of reference articles

@vindex tlon-ai-auto-proofread
When the user option @code{tlon-ai-auto-proofread} is non-nil, @code{tlon-ai-create-reference-article} automatically triggers @code{tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article} after the article has been generated. If @samp{nil} (the default), you are prompted interactively whether to proofread.

@node Task-specific models
@section Task-specific models

Each of the following user options overrides the default @samp{gptel} model for a specific task. Every option takes a cons cell of the form @samp{(BACKEND . MODEL)}, where @samp{BACKEND} is a string naming a registered @samp{gptel} backend (e.g. @samp{"Gemini"}, @samp{"ChatGPT"}) and @samp{MODEL} is a symbol identifying the model (e.g. @samp{gemini-flash-latest}, @samp{gpt-4.5-preview}). Consult @code{gptel-extras-ai-models} for the full list of available backends and models. When an option is @samp{nil}, the buffer-local or global @code{gptel-model} is used instead.

@vindex tlon-ai-summarization-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-summarization-model} controls which model generates abstracts, synopses, and meta descriptions. Because some works exceed 100,000 tokens, you should choose a model with a context window of at least one million tokens. The default is @samp{("Gemini" . gemini-flash-latest)}.

@vindex tlon-ai-markdown-fix-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-markdown-fix-model} controls which model restores Markdown formatting lost during translation (@ref{Fixing Markdown formatting, , fixing Markdown formatting}). The default is @samp{("Gemini" . gemini-flash-latest)}.

@vindex tlon-ai-create-reference-article-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-create-reference-article-model} controls which model drafts reference articles (@ref{Creating a reference article, , creating reference articles}). The default is @samp{nil} (use the global model).

@vindex tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article-model} controls which model proofreads reference articles (@ref{Proofreading a reference article, , proofreading reference articles}). Proofreading benefits from a model with strong factual reasoning. The default is @samp{("ChatGPT" . gpt-4.5-preview)}.

@vindex tlon-ai-summarize-commit-diffs-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-summarize-commit-diffs-model} controls which model summarizes commit diffs (@ref{Summarizing commit diffs, , summarizing commit diffs}). The default is @samp{("Gemini" . gemini-pro-latest)}.

@vindex tlon-ai-help-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-help-model} controls which model answers documentation-based help queries (@ref{Asking for help, , asking for help}). The default is @samp{("Gemini" . gemini-flash-latest)}.

@vindex tlon-ai-translation-model
The user option @code{tlon-ai-translation-model} controls which model performs AI-powered translation when the translate engine is set to @samp{ai}. The default is @samp{nil} (use the global model).

