@node Creating a reference article
@subsection Creating a reference article

@findex tlon-ai-create-reference-article
The command @code{tlon-ai-create-reference-article} generates an encyclopedia-style article for the Tlon effective altruism encyclopedia. It reads the @samp{title} from the YAML front matter of the current buffer, determines the article language, and constructs a prompt from @code{tlon-ai-write-reference-article-prompt}.

Before sending the request, the command collects source material. It scans the ``Further reading'' section for @samp{<Cite>} tags. For each citation, if the tag contains a @samp{locator} attribute (e.g. a chapter number), you are prompted to select the PDF that covers that specific section; otherwise, the full PDF linked in the Bib@TeX{} entry is used. All PDFs are converted to text and added to the @samp{gptel} context. A language-specific glossary is also attached when translating from English.

The generated article is placed in a new Markdown buffer. You are then offered the option to proofread it immediately (@ref{Proofreading a reference article, , proofreading}). The model can be customized via @code{tlon-ai-create-reference-article-model} (@ref{Task-specific models, , task-specific models}).

@node Proofreading a reference article
@subsection Proofreading a reference article

@findex tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article
The command @code{tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article} sends the current buffer's content to the AI for expert proofreading, focusing on factual errors, calculation mistakes, and other substantive issues. The language-appropriate prompt is drawn from @code{tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article-prompt}. The proofread version or commentary appears in a new buffer. The model can be customized via @code{tlon-ai-proofread-reference-article-model} (@ref{Task-specific models, , task-specific models}).

