@node Generating abstracts
@subsection Generating abstracts

@findex tlon-get-abstract-with-or-without-ai
The command @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-or-without-ai} is the primary entry point for obtaining an abstract. It first attempts non-AI extraction via @code{tlon-fetch-and-set-abstract} (e.g. scraping publisher metadata). If that fails, it falls back to AI generation via @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai}.

Programmatic callers may pass @samp{PRESERVE-EXISTING} to keep existing abstracts without an overwrite prompt. The policy follows AI and language-detection callbacks and checks both the live Ebib database and the visiting Bib@TeX{} buffer before writing a delayed response. Unrelated unsaved changes stop that write rather than being discarded. A changed source selection during language detection also stops processing. Interactive calls retain the configured overwrite behavior.

@findex tlon-get-abstract-with-ai
The command @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai} generates an abstract (100--250 words) using the AI@. It determines the source text from context: the region, the current buffer, or the HTML/PDF file linked in the Bib@TeX{} entry at point. The AI first checks whether the text already contains an abstract; if so, it extracts and returns it. Otherwise it creates one from scratch, ending with the phrase ``AI-generated abstract.'' The result is set as the @samp{abstract} field of the Bib@TeX{} entry, or copied to the kill ring if no Bib@TeX{} context is available. The model can be customized via @code{tlon-ai-summarization-model} (@ref{Task-specific models, , task-specific models}).

@findex tlon-shorten-abstract-with-ai
The command @code{tlon-shorten-abstract-with-ai} takes the existing @samp{abstract} field of the Bib@TeX{} entry at point and asks the AI to shorten it to the maximum length specified in @code{tlon-max-abstract-length}. The shortened abstract replaces the existing one.

@findex tlon-get-synopsis-with-ai
The command @code{tlon-get-synopsis-with-ai} generates a detailed synopsis (1000--2000 words) of the same source material that @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai} would use. The result is copied to the kill ring rather than inserted into a Bib@TeX{} field.

@findex tlon-get-abstract-with-ai-from-pdf
@findex tlon-get-abstract-with-ai-from-html
The commands @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai-from-pdf} and @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai-from-html} are convenience wrappers that call @code{tlon-get-abstract-with-ai} on the PDF or HTML file, respectively, associated with the Bib@TeX{} entry at point.

@node Generating meta descriptions
@subsection Generating meta descriptions

@findex tlon-ai-create-meta-description
The command @code{tlon-ai-create-meta-description} generates an SEO-optimized meta description (up to 160 characters) for the Markdown article in the current buffer and inserts it as the @samp{meta} field in the YAML front matter. The language is determined from the file or by prompting you. The model can be customized via @code{tlon-ai-summarization-model}.

@findex tlon-ai-create-meta-descriptions-in-directory
The command @code{tlon-ai-create-meta-descriptions-in-directory} iterates over all Markdown files in a directory, generating meta descriptions for those that do not already have a @samp{meta} field. Files whose language cannot be determined are skipped.

@node Generating titles
@subsection Generating titles

@findex tlon-ai-create-title
The command @code{tlon-ai-create-title} generates an SEO-optimized title (50--60 characters) for the article in the current buffer and inserts it as the @samp{title} field in the YAML front matter.

@node Formatting and repair
@section Formatting and repair

@menu
* Fixing Markdown formatting::
@end menu

@node Fixing Markdown formatting
@subsection Fixing Markdown formatting

@findex tlon-ai-fix-markdown-formatting
When Markdown formatting (links, emphasis, HTML elements, SSML tags) is lost or altered during translation, the command @code{tlon-ai-fix-markdown-formatting} restores it by comparing the translated file paragraph by paragraph with its original counterpart. The counterpart is identified via @code{tlon-get-counterpart}.

Paragraphs are processed concurrently (up to three at a time) with automatic retry and exponential backoff. If any paragraph permanently fails after three attempts, the entire process aborts with diagnostic information. On success, the reconstructed file is saved as @samp{[filename]--fixed.md} and you are offered an @samp{ediff} session to review the changes. The model can be customized via @code{tlon-ai-markdown-fix-model} (@ref{Task-specific models, , task-specific models}).

@node Language detection
@section Language detection

@menu
