@node Setting Bib@TeX{} language
@subsection Setting Bib@TeX{} language

@findex tlon-ai-set-language-bibtex
The command @code{tlon-ai-set-language-bibtex} detects the language of the Bib@TeX{} entry at point using AI and sets the @samp{langid} field accordingly. If a @samp{langid} field already exists and the detected language matches, no change is made. If they conflict, you are prompted to choose. If no @samp{langid} field exists, the detected value is added directly. The detected language is validated and standardized before being written.

@node Setting file language for spell-checking
@subsection Setting file language for spell-checking

@findex tlon-ai-set-language-in-file
The command @code{tlon-ai-set-language-in-file} detects the language of the current buffer or file using AI and configures the Jinx spell-checker to use that language.

@node Phonetic transcription
@section Phonetic transcription

@menu
* Transcribing text phonetically::
@end menu

@node Transcribing text phonetically
@subsection Transcribing text phonetically

@findex tlon-ai-phonetically-transcribe
The command @code{tlon-ai-phonetically-transcribe} generates an International Phonetic Alphabet (IPA) transcription of the text you provide. It defaults to the active region or word at point and determines the language from the file or by prompting you. The transcription is copied to the kill ring.

@findex tlon-phonetically-transcribe-in-buffer
The command @code{tlon-phonetically-transcribe-in-buffer} processes every line in the current buffer, appending a comma-separated IPA transcription to each line.

@node Audio transcription
@section Audio transcription

@menu
* Transcribing audio files::
@end menu

@node Transcribing audio files
@subsection Transcribing audio files

@findex tlon-transcribe-audio
The command @code{tlon-transcribe-audio} transcribes and diarizes an audio file using @samp{whisperx} locally.  It prompts for the audio file and a language code (e.g. @samp{en}, @samp{es}).  When called interactively, the transcript is displayed in a dedicated buffer.  When called programmatically with a callback, the callback receives the path to the transcript file on success or @samp{nil} on failure.

@node Mathematical expressions
@section Mathematical expressions

@menu
* Converting and translating math::
@end menu

@node Converting and translating math
@subsection Converting and translating math

@findex tlon-ai-convert-math
The command @code{tlon-ai-convert-math} converts a natural-language or plain-text mathematical expression into @LaTeX{}. If point is on a @samp{Math} tag, the @LaTeX{} result is inserted as the second value of the @samp{alt} attribute. Otherwise, the result is copied to the kill ring.

@findex tlon-ai-translate-math
The command @code{tlon-ai-translate-math} converts a @LaTeX{} expression into a natural-language description suitable for alt text (e.g. ``one half times two to the fifth power equals sixteen''). If point is on a @samp{Math} tag, the natural-language result is inserted as the first value of the @samp{alt} attribute. Otherwise, the result is copied to the kill ring.

@node Commit analysis
@section Commit analysis

@menu
* Summarizing commit diffs::
@end menu

@node Summarizing commit diffs
@subsection Summarizing commit diffs

@findex tlon-ai-summarize-commit-diffs
The command @code{tlon-ai-summarize-commit-diffs} summarizes the diffs of commits selected in a @samp{magit-log-mode} buffer. Select a region covering the commits of interest, then invoke the command. The AI produces an Org-formatted summary organized by package or feature, designed for developers who need to quickly assess breaking changes and new functionality. The summary appears in a @samp{*Commit Summary*} buffer. With a prefix argument, diffstats are included in the prompt. The model can be customized via @code{tlon-ai-summarize-commit-diffs-model} (@ref{Task-specific models, , task-specific models}).

@node Cross-repository propagation
@section Cross-repository propagation

@menu
* Propagating changes across repositories::
@end menu

@node Propagating changes across repositories
@subsection Propagating changes across repositories

@findex tlon-ai-propagate-changes
The command @code{tlon-ai-propagate-changes} automatically applies changes from a commit in the current repository to corresponding files in all other Uqbar content repositories (both originals and translations). If invoked from @samp{magit-status-mode} with point on a commit, that commit is used; otherwise, the latest commit is used.

For each modified file in the source commit, the command retrieves the diff and locates the corresponding file in each target repository via metadata lookups (@samp{original_path}). It then asks the AI to apply the semantic equivalent of the changes to the target file's content. The AI response overwrites the target file and is automatically committed with a message referencing the source commit.

The command requires a clean working tree (no uncommitted changes) and relies on consistent metadata across repositories.

@node Documentation-based help
@section Documentation-based help

@menu
* Asking for help::
@end menu

@node Asking for help
@subsection Asking for help

@findex tlon-ai-ask-for-help
The command @code{tlon-ai-ask-for-help} lets you ask a free-form question about the Tlon ecosystem. It collects documentation files---@samp{.org} files from the @samp{doc/} directories of the @samp{tlon} and @samp{extras} repositories, readme files from Tlon-related repos, and the user's @samp{config.org}---and adds them to the @samp{gptel} context. Your question, together with this context, is sent to the model specified by @code{tlon-ai-help-model}. The answer appears in a new @samp{gptel-mode} buffer. You are then prompted to clear the context; if you have follow-up questions, you can decline and clear manually later with @code{gptel-context-remove-all}.

@node Transient menu
@section Transient menu

@findex tlon-ai-menu
The command @code{tlon-ai-menu} opens a comprehensive transient menu that exposes all AI operations and their associated options. The menu is organized into three columns:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Summarize}: abstract generation (with and without AI), synopsis, meta description, and batch/overwrite options.
@item
@strong{Math / Reference articles / Propagation}: math conversion and translation, reference article creation and proofreading, commit diff summarization, and change propagation.
@item
@strong{Misc / Options / Models}: Bib@TeX{} language detection, Markdown fix, phonetic transcription, rewriting, translation, title generation, the edit-prompt toggle, debug toggle, and per-task model selection.
@end itemize

The ``Models'' section allows you to interactively select models for each task from all registered @samp{gptel} backends.

