@node Sending requests to the AI
@section Sending requests to the AI

@findex tlon-make-gptel-request
The function @code{tlon-make-gptel-request} is the central dispatch point for all AI requests in the module. It accepts a prompt string, optional printf arguments, a callback, a full model specification (as a @samp{(BACKEND . MODEL)} cons cell), and optional parameters for tools, MCP servers, and request buffers. It pins the selected backend and model buffer-locally so that follow-up tool calls reuse the same provider. All other commands in this module delegate to this function.

@node Callback utilities
@section Callback utilities

@findex tlon-ai-callback-return
@findex tlon-ai-callback-copy
@findex tlon-ai-callback-save
@findex tlon-ai-callback-insert
@findex tlon-ai-callback-fail
The module provides a family of generic callback functions for common response-handling patterns:

@itemize
@item
@code{tlon-ai-callback-return} returns the response string.
@item
@code{tlon-ai-callback-copy} copies the response to the kill ring and messages it.
@item
@code{tlon-ai-callback-save} saves the response to a file.
@item
@code{tlon-ai-callback-insert} inserts the response at the position where the request was sent.
@item
@code{tlon-ai-callback-fail} displays an error message extracted from the response info.
@end itemize

@node Retrieving text content
@section Retrieving text content

@findex tlon-get-string-dwim
The function @code{tlon-get-string-dwim} (``Do What I Mean'') returns text content from the most appropriate source. If a region is active, it returns the region text. In @samp{bibtex-mode} or @samp{ebib-entry-mode}, it returns the contents of the HTML or PDF file linked in the Bib@TeX{} entry. In @samp{pdf-view-mode} or @samp{eww-mode}, it returns the current document's contents. In @samp{markdown-mode}, it returns the substantive content (excluding metadata). Otherwise, it returns the full buffer contents. Many AI commands use this function to determine what to send to the model.

@findex tlon-get-file-as-string
The function @code{tlon-get-file-as-string} reads a file into a string, handling PDF-to-Markdown conversion and HTML-to-text rendering via @samp{eww} transparently.

@node Translation helpers
@section Translation helpers

@findex tlon-ai-translate-text
The function @code{tlon-ai-translate-text} translates a text string from one language to another, attaching a glossary when translating from English. It manages its own temporary request buffer and cleans up glossary files after the callback completes.

@findex tlon-ai-request-wrapper
The function @code{tlon-ai-request-wrapper} provides the integration point for the @samp{tlon-translate} machinery, dispatching AI-backed translation requests with automatic glossary handling and buffer management.

